    "rich_text_6aeaLY": {
      "type": "rich_text",
      "name": "Case Studies in Detail",
      "settings": {
        "richtext_inhalt": "<h3>CASE STUDIES IN DETAIL</h3><p><strong>EMPLOYEE ONBOARDING – FIRST IMPRESSIONS COUNT</strong></p><p>The onboarding kit is one of the most significant touchpoints in the employee experience. What a new employee receives on their first day has a lasting impact on their perception of the company. A high-quality, branded bag or case featuring the company logo sends a clear message: This company invests in its staff; it has high standards of quality and consistency.</p><p>For resellers, this is a business model that repeats automatically with every new hire. If the branded onboarding kit is part of the standard process, there is a guaranteed order for every new employee – no need for acquisition, no pitching, no competition.</p><p><strong><br/>SALES & FIELD STAFF – BRAND AMBASSADORS IN THE FIELD</strong></p><p>Field staff, consultants and sales teams are a company’s most visible representatives when dealing with customers. What they wear and carry forms part of the professional impression they make. A uniform, branded bag or case signals: this company has standards – and adheres to them.</p><p>For many companies, this is also a security issue: if 50 field staff members carry the same branded case, it is immediately clear at a glance who belongs to the team and who does not. In security-sensitive environments, this is a practical benefit, not merely an aesthetic consideration.</p><p><strong><br/>EVENTS & TRADE FAIRS – MERCHANDISE WITH ADDED VALUE</strong></p><p>Trade fair appearances and corporate events are classic occasions for branded merchandise. The challenge is that most merchandise items – pens, notebooks, water bottles – end up in a cupboard or are thrown away after a short time. A high-quality laptop sleeve or a branded rucksack has a different lifespan: it is used every day, is visible and regularly reminds the wearer of the brand.</p><p>For resellers, this is a selling point when dealing with marketing managers: ‘The DICOTA sleeve costs more than a pen – but your customers use it every day and see your logo every time. This is measurably more effective than traditional event merchandise.’</p><p><strong><br/>CORPORATE ROLL-OUT – ONE ORDER, GLOBAL PRESENCE</strong></p><p>Large corporations with global offices standardise their equipment worldwide – including accessories. If a company with 10,000 employees decides that all laptops should have the same branded case, that represents an order for 10,000 units – and potentially a recurring annual order due to new hires and device replacements.</p><p>DICOTA has the production capacity for such high-volume orders and the experience in global delivery. For resellers managing such accounts, this is a strategic selling point: “I have a partner who can produce 10,000 customised cases and deliver them worldwide – within the agreed lead time and to a consistent standard of quality.”</p>",
        "width": "narrow",
        "padding_top": 4,
        "padding_bottom": 4
      }
    },
